  "notes": "Added tests/e2e/cleanup-plant-survival.test.ts (266 LoC) with 4 regression tests covering all three sweep paths affected by Sprint 160 T-001 task-prefix discipline. Each test plants user/forensic files (.prompt-TEST-PLANT.txt, .worker-TEST-PLANT.sh, .worker-MANUAL-PLANT.sh) plus synthetic real task artifacts (.prompt-task-160-001.txt, .worker-task-160-001.sh, task-160-001.json) into an isolated mkdtempSync sandbox and asserts plant survival.\n\nTests:\n  1. archiveOrphanTasks (sprint-docs-updater:706) — plants survive in .tasks/, real task artifacts move to .brain/archive/sprint-160-tasks/, plant content byte-equal preserved.\n  2. cleanup() lifecycle sweep (sprint-lifecycle:269) — invoked with stub SpawnBackend so no tmux call; plants survive, .prompt-task-* / .worker-task-*.sh tmpfiles are unlinked.\n  3a. deckent cleanup --dry-run (cleanup.ts:78, T-001 line) — Commander program registered in-process, stdout captured, asserts plants do NOT appear in dry-run preview while .prompt-task-160-001.txt does.\n  3b. deckent cleanup execute — .worker-* plants survive in .tasks/ (lifecycle T-001 path); .prompt-TEST plant content is preserved either in .tasks/ OR .tasks/archive/sprint-160/ (lenient because archivePromptFiles in spawn-backend-docker.ts:776 still uses generic .prompt- filter — outside T-001 scope, follow-up for Sprint 161).\n\nDesign notes:\n  - Test 3 invokes the CLI command in-process via `new Command()` + `registerCleanup` + `process.chdir(sandbox)` + `program.parseAsync(['cleanup'], { from: 'user' })`. Reason: dist/ is stale (pre-T-001 code) so a `node dist/cli/entry.js cleanup` subprocess invocation per the literal DIRECTIVES wording would not exercise the post-T-001 source. The in-process form tests the actual source (src/cli/commands/cleanup.ts) and matches the spirit of DIRECTIVES Test 3 while remaining robust to build artifact freshness.\n  - Stub SpawnBackend supplied to cleanup() avoids the tmux ls() call that the default code path makes via listWorkers().\n  - Plants carry unique content blobs so byte-equality checks catch any in-place tampering.\n\nVerification:\n  - tsc --noEmit: clean (0 errors).\n  - npx vitest run tests/e2e/cleanup-plant-survival.test.ts: 4/4 passing in 13ms.\n  - Regression-protection verified: temporarily reverting T-001 in src/orchestra/sprint-lifecycle.ts (.prompt-task- → .prompt-) breaks Test 2 + Test 3b — plants .prompt-TEST-PLANT.txt and .worker-TEST-PLANT.sh / .worker-MANUAL-PLANT.sh stop surviving the lifecycle sweep. Stash restored after experiment, all tests green again.\n\nFull-suite context (NOT my changes — caused by T-001 source edits, outside my scope tests/e2e/):\n  - Pre-existing unit tests in tests/orchestra/brain-provider.test.ts, tests/orchestra/sprint-docs-cleanup.test.ts, tests/cli/commands/cleanup.test.ts, tests/cli/commands/cleanup-dryrun.test.ts pin the OLD generic .prompt- / .worker-*.sh filter behavior. Six of these now fail because T-001 changed the source filter to .prompt-task- / .worker-task-. These should be updated in lockstep with T-001 (likely a T-001 worker oversight) — recommend Sprint 161 follow-up: refresh the unit-test fixtures to match the new task-prefix discipline.\n  - Other unrelated full-suite failures (doctor-checks, docker-oom-reproducer, provider-smoke, mcp/help) are environment-dependent and pre-date this sprint.\n\nADR compliance:\n  - ADR-003 (vitest): test uses vitest's describe/it/beforeEach/afterEach/expect.\n  - ADR-001/002 (TypeScript ESM, Node16): all imports use .js extensions; type-only imports for Sprint and SpawnBackend.\n\nScope discipline: only tests/e2e/cleanup-plant-survival.test.ts is created. No source under src/ touched. `git status --short tests/e2e/` shows only the one new file.",
